# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rust / Cargo
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Build output. One workspace at the repo root, so `/target` covers the
# real one; `**/target/` catches nested builds under examples/ and any
# user module a test fixture happens to `cargo build` in place.
/target
**/target/

# NOTE: Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This workspace ships an
# executable (the `sb` binary), and the lockfile is what makes a release
# build reproducible — installguide.md pins zenoh 1.9 / iceoryx2 0.9 and
# relies on it. Only *library* crates ignore their lockfile.
Cargo.lock.bak

# rustfmt backups
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC debug symbols. Release builds emit target/<triple>/release/sb.pdb
# (9.8 MB at v0.1.29) — already covered by /target, but a stray copy left
# next to a hand-run binary should not be committed either.
*.pdb

# Coverage / profiling
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage/
/tarpaulin-report.*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build switch
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Per-dev-box platform selector (OS=windows|linux|mac). Copy .env.example
# to .env. See installguide_windows.md §2.
/.env

# Release artifacts under platforms/*/dist/ are deliberately NOT ignored —
# they are the record of what shipped. See platforms/README.md.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated message-vault artifacts
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `sb message compile` writes a protobuf descriptor cache and per-backend
# bindings into the vault. Sources are the .proto files only; everything
# below is regenerable and is excluded from the release payload too
# (installguide.md step 4 rsync).
message_definitions/.cache/
message_definitions/targets/

# Defensive: older layouts emitted bindings alongside the .proto they came
# from rather than under targets/.
message_definitions/**/*.rs
message_definitions/**/*.h
message_definitions/**/*.py

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.claude/
.claude.json
.claude.local.json
.mcp.json
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md

# ...except project skills, which encode repo-wide invariants (e.g.
# /sb-release owns the seven-way version mirror). A teammate without them
# would bump versions by hand and break the build's drift check.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS cruft
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scratch
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/tmp/
*.log
